# App Router Conventions

- `src/app` contains routing concerns only: `page`, `layout`, metadata, and server actions.
- Keep route files minimal; delegate to module pages in `src/modules/<scope>/pages/*`.
- Use global boundaries at app root when possible (`src/app/loading.tsx`, `src/app/error.tsx`, `src/app/not-found.tsx`).

## Required patterns

- Redirect/auth checks in server layout/page boundaries where possible.
- Keep route segment naming consistent and lower-case.
- Prefer direct imports to module page files, no route-entry intermediates.

## Prohibited patterns

- Large feature-specific UI trees directly inside route files.
- Business state orchestration spread across multiple `page.tsx` files.
- Route imports that depend on `route-entry` folders.
